T:call-clock-#-#-utc = Clock: #:# UTC
T:call-clock-tuesday-#-#-# = Clock: Tuesday #-#-#, #:# UTC
T:call-context-manager-cm = Context Manager: [CM] Recall memory L#-#.
T:call-context-manager-system = Context Manager: System: You will soon form a new memory, get ready. The messages that follow are the slice of recent experience you are about to compress. After them, write the memory in your own voice.
T:call-context-manager-write-70b71121 = Context Manager: Write the memory of events since the most recent memory system notification. Speak in the first person from your own perspective. Preserve concrete details — file paths, exact values, decisions, unresolved questions, the user's active asks. Target ~# tokens. Output only the memory body — no preamble, no section headers unless they help preservation, no meta-commentary about summarizing. Memorize only what actually happened in that slice: if it holds little beyond routine system traffic (heartbeats, empty turns, failure notices), a short memory saying so is correct — do not pad it by re-narrating events you already remember from earlier as if they had just happened again.
  
  Write the memory directly as plain prose — do not wrap it in <thinking> or any other tags; begin immediately with the memory text itself.
T:call-context-manager-write-7f24f266 = Context Manager: Write the memory of events since the most recent memory system notification. Speak in the first person from your own perspective. Preserve concrete details — file paths, exact values, decisions, unresolved questions, the user's active asks. Target ~# tokens. Output only the memory body — no preamble, no section headers unless they help preservation, no meta-commentary about summarizing. Memorize only what actually happened in that slice: if it holds little beyond routine system traffic (heartbeats, empty turns, failure notices), a short memory saying so is correct — do not pad it by re-narrating events you already remember from earlier as if they had just happened again.
T:call-context-manager-you-have-just-reviewed-the-l# = Context Manager: You have just reviewed the L# memories above, in chronological order. They cover the stretch of experience you are about to consolidate into a single L# memory. Write a memory that preserves the through-line: what happened, what was decided, what remains open, what concrete details future you will want to reach for. Speak in the first person. Target ~# tokens. Output only the memory body — no preamble, no meta-commentary about summarizing.
T:call-context-manager-you-have-just-reviewed-the-slices = Context Manager: You have just reviewed the slices of recent experience above (raw conversation), in chronological order. They cover the stretch of experience you are about to consolidate into a single L# memory. Write a memory that preserves the through-line: what happened, what was decided, what remains open, what concrete details future you will want to reach for. Speak in the first person. Target ~# tokens. Output only the memory body — no preamble, no meta-commentary about summarizing.
T:call-empty = 
  
